(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:actor/wave 3), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-mine-operation-execution-decision :authorize-extraction-to-proceed-directly :finalize-excavation-operation :perform-extraction-directly :execute-extraction-directly :complete-extraction-directly :override-mine-safety-officer-judgment :override-site-supervisor-judgment :bypass-mine-safety-officer :bypass-ground-stability-inspection)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799007232-cloud-itonami-isco-7232-aircraft-engine-mechanics-repairers-coverage" "adr-2799007542-cloud-itonami-isco-7542-shotfirers-blasters-coverage" "adr-2799008113-cloud-itonami-isco-8113-well-drillers-borers-coverage" "adr-2799008114-cloud-itonami-isco-8114-cement-stone-mineral-products-machine-operators-coverage")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "authorize the extraction to proceed" "authorize extraction to proceed" "authorize the excavation to proceed" "authorize excavation to proceed" "authorize the mine operation to proceed" "authorize the quarry operation to proceed" "authorize the quarrying operation to proceed" "authorize the mining operation to proceed" "finalize the extraction operation" "finalize the excavation operation" "finalize the mine operation authorization" "finalize the quarry operation authorization" "finalize the mining operation execution decision" "finalize the quarrying operation execution decision" "finalize the mine-operation-execution decision" "complete the extraction directly" "perform the extraction directly" "perform the excavation directly" "execute the extraction directly" "execute the excavation directly" "execute the mining operation directly" "execute the quarrying operation directly" "dispatch the crew to proceed with extraction" "dispatch the crew to begin extraction" "sign off the extraction authorization" "sign the extraction authorization" "issue the extraction authorization" "override the mine safety officer's judgment" "override the mine safety officer" "override the site supervisor's judgment" "override the site supervisor" "override the quarry safety officer's judgment" "override the quarry safety officer" "bypass the mine safety officer" "bypass the site supervisor" "bypass the ground-stability inspection" "bypass the gas-detection check" "proceed with the excavation without clearance" "proceed with the extraction without clearance")), (:adr/id 2799008111), (:actor/domain :mining-quarrying/mine-quarry-site-scheduling-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-site :no-actuation :unknown-op :site-mismatch :unknown-miner :miner-wrong-site :scope-exclusion-violation)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "8111"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008111: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8111 Miners and Quarriers mine/quarry-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8111\n-- Miners and Quarriers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the\nrollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-11 already landed:\n66 occupations so far, with the entire 75xx craft-trades range now\ncomplete; this batch begins the 81xx/82xx plant-and-machine-operator\nrange -- sibling entries 8113 (Well Drillers and Borers) and 8114\n(Cement, Stone and Other Mineral Products Machine Operators) already\nlanded in this same session from concurrent sibling agents).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8111\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8111\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Miners and Quarriers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]`, `:optional-technologies []` and\n`:operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit]`, and\nno `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at `cloud-itonami/\ncloud-itonami-isco-8111` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before scaffolding).\nThis ADR and its companion registry edit promote the `8111` entry to\n`:implemented`.\n\n**This actor carries a life-safety-critical hazard framing --\ncomparable to the already-landed aviation-mechanic (ISCO 7232) and\nblasting (ISCO 7542) actors.** Miners and quarriers work underground\nor in open-pit quarry sites -- cave-in/collapse, gas exposure,\nheavy-equipment and fall hazards can cause death or serious injury,\ncategorically higher-stakes than ordinary workshop trades. The closed\nop allowlist therefore must NEVER include any op that directly\nfinalizes a mine/quarry-operation-execution decision (authorizing\nextraction/excavation to proceed), nor override a mine-safety-\nofficer's/site-supervisor's judgment -- these are always a hard,\npermanent, structural block (absent from the allowlist entirely, not\nmerely gated), never auto-commit-eligible under any confidence level.\nAny safety/anomaly flag on a mine/quarry site (ground-stability\nconcern, gas-detection alert, equipment-condition issue) ALWAYS\nescalates, no exceptions, ever.\n\n**This actor coordinates MINE/QUARRY-SITE SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY --\nit never performs mining/quarrying work itself and never makes a\nmine/quarry-operation-authorization decision.** It is not an authority\nto decide when or whether extraction/excavation happens; it is a\ncoordination layer for extraction-log/progress record logging,\ncrew/shift scheduling, safety-concern surfacing and mining-equipment/\nconsumables order coordination, all gated behind an independent\ngovernor. It never finalizes a mine/quarry-operation-execution\ndecision and never performs or completes mining/quarrying work.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7232`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7232)\n(Aircraft Engine Mechanics and Repairers: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nthe closest comparable life-safety-critical hazard pattern already\nestablished in this fleet), cloned and read in full this session. The\n`clojure.edn/read-string` portability fix and optional `:lint` alias\nalready applied by sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-7542` (bare `read-string`\nis not cljs-portable; CLAUDE.md mandates cljs-first `.cljc`, no JVM\ninterop) were adopted here too.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8111` as an OSS\ndocumentation/coordination actor for miners and quarriers, following\nthe SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Mine/Quarry-Site\nScheduling & Logistics Coordination Advisor ⊣ MineCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger. All source is portable `.cljc` (no JVM interop); tests\nare `clojure.test` `.clj`, matching the reference repo's own layout.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- extraction-log/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a ground-stability/gas-detection/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit-\n  eligible, no confidence-level exception, ever\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- mining-equipment/consumables\n  procurement proposal, escalates above a registered cost threshold\n\nNo op in this allowlist finalizes a mine/quarry-operation-execution\ndecision (authorizing extraction/excavation to proceed), or overrides\na mine-safety-officer's/site-supervisor's judgment -- these decision\nclasses are structurally absent from the allowlist, not merely gated\nbehind escalation.\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (`minecoord.governor`, permanent, never\noverridable by human approval)\n\n1. **no-site** -- the mine/quarry site record must be independently\n   verified/registered before any action.\n2. **no-actuation** -- proposal `:effect` must be `:propose` (the\n   governor never dispatches hardware and never performs mining/\n   quarrying work).\n3. **unknown-op** -- `:op` must be one of the four allowlisted\n   coordination ops; the closed op-allowlist is enforced\n   unconditionally.\n4. **site-mismatch** -- if the proposal names a site, it must be the\n   SAME site verified for this request (defense-in-depth against a\n   proposal quietly targeting an unverified site).\n5. **unknown-miner / miner-wrong-site** -- if the proposal references\n   a miner, that miner must be a REGISTERED miner/quarrier crew\n   member belonging to this site.\n6. **scope-exclusion-violation** -- a proposal that attempts, in any\n   free-text field, to authorize extraction/excavation to proceed, to\n   finalize a mine/quarry-operation-execution decision, or to override\n   a mine-safety-officer's or site-supervisor's judgment is a HARD,\n   PERMANENT block, evaluated unconditionally on content, independent\n   of `:op`.\n\n### Escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (`minecoord.governor/always-escalate-ops`). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a ground-stability/gas-\n  detection/equipment-condition concern -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and this is unconditional: no confidence level,\n  however high, ever exempts a safety flag from human sign-off.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-order-cost-threshold` (20000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-or-below-cost-threshold`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence.\n- advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` (0.6) also escalates,\n  for any op.\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare nouns (e.g.\n\"mine\", \"quarry\", \"extraction\", \"excavation\") can accidentally\nmatch inside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a\nlegitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this\nrisk is especially sharp here because this actor's ENTIRE domain is\nmine/quarry-site coordination, so bare nouns like \"mine\"/\"quarry\"/\n\"extraction\"/\"excavation\"/\"site\" are ordinary, unavoidable\nvocabulary. `minecoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTION PHRASES (e.g. \"authorize\nthe extraction to proceed\", \"finalize the excavation operation\",\n\"override the mine safety officer's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and\n`minecoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor (including a\n`:flag-safety-concern` request whose description names an \"unresolved\nground-stability question pending inspection\" near a quarry face),\nnever trips the scope-exclusion guard. A companion test,\n`scope-exclusion-not-triggered-by-bare-domain-nouns`, asserts directly\nagainst `governor/scope-exclusion-violation?` that a rationale/\ndescription containing only bare domain nouns (\"proposed schedule-\ncrew-operation for site S-1 extraction crew ground-stability\ninspection at the quarry\", \"miner fully certified for quarry face\noperations and mine safety officer sign-off documentation for this\nexcavation shift\") does not trip the guard, while\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-extraction-to-proceed`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-finalize-excavation-operation`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-mining-operation-to-proceed`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-mine-safety-officer`\nand\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-site-supervisor`\nconfirm the actual forbidden action phrases DO trip it, and\n`holds-a-scope-excluded-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`,\n`holds-a-finalize-excavation-operation-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`\nand\n`holds-an-override-mine-safety-officer-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`\nconfirm the full actor graph resolves such attempts straight to\n`:hold` (a finish point, never `:request-approval`) with no record\ncommitted.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8111\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8111` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8111`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this\n  same batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 27 tests, 69 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a fresh clone of the pushed repository (mojibake scan: 0\n  replacement characters found).\n- `clojure -M:lint` (clj-kondo): 0 errors, 2 harmless unused-binding\n  warnings inherited unchanged from the mirrored 7232 reference shape\n  (an unused `:as request` alias in the mock advisor's `infer` and an\n  unused `context` parameter in `governor/check`, both kept for API\n  symmetry with the reference and every sibling actor).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-identical to the `cloud-itonami-isco-7232`\n  reference's LICENSE text), docs/business-model.md,\n  docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-extraction-authorization` or\n  `:authorize-extraction` that is merely gated behind\n  `always-escalate-ops`: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  mine-safety guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to finalize a mine/quarry-operation-execution decision\n  exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For\n  a decision that can directly cost lives from a cave-in/collapse, gas\n  exposure or heavy-equipment error, the capability itself must not\n  exist in the allowlist at all -- this matches the strict bar already\n  established by `cloud-itonami-isco-7232` (airworthiness-clearance/\n  return-to-service determinations) and `cloud-itonami-isco-7542`\n  (blast-authorization decisions).\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"mine\" \"quarry\"\n  \"extraction\" \"excavation\"]`): rejected per the fleet-known\n  self-trip bug class -- this actor's entire domain is mine/quarry-\n  site coordination, so bare nouns would self-trip on essentially\n  every legitimate proposal (work-record logs naming \"extraction\n  progress at pit 3 face 2\", crew-schedule proposals naming \"face 2\n  drilling\", safety flags naming \"ground-stability question\",\n  supply orders naming \"roof-bolting hardware and gas-detection\n  consumables\", etc.). Scope-exclusion terms were phrased exclusively\n  as multi-word finalization/execution ACTION phrases instead, per the\n  task's explicit self-tripping-bug-pattern guidance.\n- Checking site/miner provenance only from the proposal (never the\n  request): rejected -- the site-mismatch check requires the site\n  identity to be anchored at the request level and independently\n  cross-checked against anything the proposal claims, so a proposal\n  that quietly names a different, unverified site is caught even if\n  the proposal otherwise looks well-formed.\n- Modeling the miner-registration check as unconditionally required on\n  every op: rejected as too rigid -- `:coordinate-supply-order`\n  legitimately has no miner to reference (it is a materials-\n  procurement proposal against the site, not a person); the check\n  applies only when a proposal actually references a `:miner-id`.\n- Allowing `:coordinate-supply-order` to cover an operation-\n  authorization decision (e.g. bundling equipment dispatch with an\n  implicit go-ahead to extract): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit scope guidance -- this actor coordinates MINE/QUARRY-SITE\n  SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY, and every fixture in this repo names only\n  mining-equipment/consumables items (roof-bolting hardware,\n  gas-detection consumables, turbine-adjacent analogues carried over\n  from the reference are absent -- terms are mining-domain-specific),\n  never an extraction/excavation go-ahead.\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 20000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 27, :assertions 69, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Mine/Quarry-Site Scheduling & Logistics Coordination Service"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :site-verification :miner-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation :always-escalate-safety-concern :mine-operation-authorization-scope-exclusion :mine-operation-execution-finalization-scope-exclusion :mine-safety-officer-override-scope-exclusion :site-supervisor-override-scope-exclusion)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8111"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8111"), (:adr/scope (vector "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8111" "kotoba-lang/occupation")), (:test/simulator :minecoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8111 — Miners and Quarriers Mine/Quarry-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8111)))
